# Copy to .env.local for local work (gitignored), and set the same keys in the
# Vercel project's environment variables for the deployment.
#
# SERVER-SIDE ONLY. Never prefix any of these with VITE_ - Vite copies every
# VITE_-prefixed variable into the public browser bundle, which for these would
# publish write access to the live game config to anyone who opens the page.
#
# Changing a variable in Vercel does nothing until the next deploy. Redeploy.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- ConfigCat --
# Management API (a.k.a. Public API) credentials. From the ConfigCat dashboard:
# account menu (top right) -> "Public API credentials" -> add a new credential.
# You get a Basic auth user name and password pair; the password is shown once.
CONFIGCAT_API_USER=
CONFIGCAT_API_PASS=

# Optional. Default to the Cliff Heroes product and its CliffHeroes config.
# CONFIGCAT_PRODUCT_ID=
# CONFIGCAT_CONFIG_ID=

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- GitHub --
# Records every publish in config/, and is where the scheduler keeps its
# schedules and per-config fallbacks. Publishing works without it and says the
# history was not written; scheduling does not work without it at all.
#
# It must be a fine-grained personal access token whose RESOURCE OWNER is the
# organisation that owns the repository - a token created under a personal
# account cannot reach an organisation repository however its permissions are
# set - with Contents: Read and write on this repository only. An organisation
# owner then has to approve it under the organisation's Settings -> Personal
# access tokens -> Pending requests.
#
# GET /api/git/status reports exactly which of those is wrong, and the
# Overview page renders it.
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# Optional. Default to OffStarsStudios/cliff-heroes-arena-exporter and main.
# GITHUB_REPO=
# GITHUB_BRANCH=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Scheduler --
# Guards POST /api/schedule/tick when set, and leaves it open when not. Open is
# defensible - a tick can only apply a window whose start time has passed, so it
# can never publish something that was not already going to be published - but
# set it anyway.
#
# The same value goes in this repository's Actions secrets, alongside
# BACK_OFFICE_URL, for .github/workflows/schedule-tick.yml. That workflow is the
# real heartbeat; the cron in vercel.json is a once-a-day backstop.
CRON_SECRET=
